## Verdict rationale
Default-to-FAIL-on-ambiguity does not even apply here — the vanish case is
deterministic and reproduced twice (yearly and monthly variants). This is a
real, user-visible correctness gap in the delivered fix (an imminent
recurring debit can still be silently omitted from the projection on
non-UTC hosts), directly contradicting the claim under test. Recommend
sending back to the worker: either compare using each side's UTC-normalized
calendar day (not each value's own Location) so write/read semantics attach
to a single, unambiguous "today" boundary, or otherwise close the
asOfDay-exclusion boundary explicitly against occ's real instant rather than
its label.
